What color dress are you going to wear down the aisle?
你打算穿着什么颜色的裙子走红毯？

594
00:30:06.790 --> 00:30:08.170
Okay, that's Angela.
好吧, 那是安吉拉。

595
00:30:08.430 --> 00:30:09.150
That's right.
没错。

596
00:30:11.110 --> 00:30:11.670
Okay.
好的。

597
00:30:12.130 --> 00:30:18.490
Some people think that buffets are cheap, but I actually prefer them over the small portions of a fancy sit-down dinner.
有些人觉得自助餐很廉价, 但比起高级正餐那种分量极少的小盘菜, 我其实更喜欢自助餐。

598
00:30:19.850 --> 00:30:22.150
Oh, I don't know that one.
哦, 这个我不知道是谁写的。

599
00:30:22.310 --> 00:30:23.670
Someone who's into food.
一个是个老饕。

600
00:30:24.470 --> 00:30:28.830
But that feels like, um, is that like, uh, I don't know.
但这感觉像是个, 嗯, 这算是个, 嗯, 我不知道。

601
00:30:29.550 --> 00:30:30.990
That is Kevin.
那是凯文。

602
00:30:31.570 --> 00:30:32.650
Oh, Kevin.
哦，凯文。

603
00:30:33.370 --> 00:30:34.990
Okay, one more, one more.
好吧，再来一个，再来一个。

604
00:30:35.250 --> 00:30:36.410
That could have been Creed.
那也可能是克里德。

605
00:30:36.650 --> 00:30:38.010
I feel like that could have been Creed.
我觉得那也可能是克里德。

606
00:30:38.210 --> 00:30:39.790
Food-related could have been Creed.
跟食物有关的可能是克里德。

607
00:30:39.790 --> 00:30:43.230
It also could have been Oscar because he's kind of frugal, right?
也可能是奥斯卡，因为他有点节俭，对吧？

608
00:30:43.310 --> 00:30:44.150
True, true.
没错，没错。

609
00:30:44.150 --> 00:30:44.650
All right.
好了。

610
00:30:45.030 --> 00:30:46.190
Here's the last one.
这是最后一个。

611
00:30:47.270 --> 00:30:50.770
Pam, you are like a daughter to me, and Jim is like a son.
帕姆，你就像我的女儿一样，吉姆就像我的儿子。

612
00:30:51.130 --> 00:30:53.750
I'm so proud that my son and daughter are to be wed.
我为我的儿子和女儿即将结为连理感到无比自豪。

613
00:30:53.970 --> 00:30:55.110
Tis a thing of beauty.
这真是一件美妙的事。

614
00:30:55.350 --> 00:30:56.030
Glory be.
赞美主。

615
00:30:56.590 --> 00:30:58.270
I think that's Michael Scott.
我觉得那是迈克尔·斯科特。

616
00:30:58.470 --> 00:30:59.170
That's right.
没错。

617
00:30:59.610 --> 00:31:00.010
Aw.
噢。

618
00:31:00.250 --> 00:31:01.370
You did really good.
你做得真好。

619
00:31:01.870 --> 00:31:02.670
I did.
我确实做得好。

620
00:31:03.110 --> 00:31:05.170
I know my wedding guests, I guess.
我想我挺了解我的婚礼来宾的。

621
00:31:05.310 --> 00:31:05.990
You really do.
你确实很了解。

622
00:31:06.670 --> 00:31:12.550
Well, listen, lady, I think we should take a break, and then we will really get into this part two of Niagara.
听着，女士，我觉得我们应该休息一下，然后我们就要正式进入《尼亚加拉瀑布》的第二部分了。

623
00:31:12.830 --> 00:31:14.750
I've got a lot of cool stuff, I think.
我想我有很多很酷的料。

624
00:31:15.050 --> 00:31:15.910
Let's do it.
我们开始吧。

625
00:31:15.910 --> 00:31:40.080
We are back, and we open with Andy riding in pain in her hotel room because Pam's the only sober person who can take him to the hospital for his torn scrotum.
我们回来了，开场是安迪在酒店房间里痛得直叫，因为帕姆是唯一一个清醒的人，能带他去医院看他撕裂的阴囊。

626
00:31:40.800 --> 00:31:40.940
Yeah.
是啊。

627
00:31:41.180 --> 00:31:45.840
She tries to call Jim to help her, but he's clearly drunky Jim.
她试图打电话叫吉姆帮忙，但他显然是喝醉的吉姆。

628
00:31:46.840 --> 00:31:52.220
Jenna, this was a much bigger storyline that would have really shown Jim's night and where he was at.
珍娜，原本这是一个更大篇幅的故事线，本可以真正展现吉姆当晚的经历和他的状态。

629
00:31:52.220 --> 00:31:59.020
In fact, there was a talking head where he explained their night of drinking, and I think you need to hear it.
事实上，原本有一个面对镜头的独白环节，他解释了他们喝酒的那个夜晚，我觉得你必须听听。

630
00:31:59.440 --> 00:31:59.920
What?
什么？

631
00:32:00.260 --> 00:32:00.620
Yeah.
是啊。

632
00:32:00.880 --> 00:32:01.940
In deleted scenes.
在删减片段里。

633
00:32:02.100 --> 00:32:02.680
Let's hear it.
我们听听看。

634
00:32:03.240 --> 00:32:06.120
A bunch of us decided to go over the border to Canada for one quick drink.
我们一群人决定过境去加拿大喝一杯。

635
00:32:06.480 --> 00:32:08.900
So I'm in a car with Michael and Dwight.
所以我跟迈克尔和德怀特坐在一辆车里。

636
00:32:09.740 --> 00:32:13.760
When we get to the border, Dwight refuses to relinquish his sidearm.
当我们到达边境时，德怀特拒绝交出他的随身武器。

637
00:32:13.960 --> 00:32:17.240
So 40 minutes later, here we are.
所以40分钟后，我们就落得这般田地。

638
00:32:18.460 --> 00:32:18.940
Wow.
哇。

639
00:32:19.300 --> 00:32:19.560
Yeah.
是啊。

640
00:32:19.560 --> 00:32:27.040
Greg said in the commentary there were more scenes of the guys' night out, that they even, like, get Oscar in, and they're going to go to a club.
格雷格在评论音轨里说过，还有更多关于这几个男人之夜的场景，他们甚至还拉上了奥斯卡，打算去一家俱乐部。

641
00:32:27.300 --> 00:32:31.280
Like, it was a whole thing, but it ended up just being the scenes you see in the episode.
就像这样，原本是一整套情节，但最后播出的只有你在剧集里看到的那些场景。

642
00:32:31.580 --> 00:32:32.640
Oh, wow.
哦，哇。

643
00:32:33.340 --> 00:32:40.800
Well, Pam does end up driving Andy to the hospital, and Angela, I just want to point out Pam's glasses that she's wearing.
嗯，帕姆最后确实开车送安迪去了医院，安杰拉，我只想指出帕姆戴的那副眼镜。

644
00:32:40.800 --> 00:32:46.420
I thought this was a great callback to the fact that she wears glasses at all.
我觉得这很好地呼应了她其实会戴眼镜这一设定。

645
00:32:46.600 --> 00:32:50.160
And remember, we had the episode where she wears her backup glasses to work.
而且大家还记得吧，我们曾有过一集，她戴着备用眼镜去上班。

646
00:32:50.320 --> 00:32:50.660
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

647
00:32:51.000 --> 00:32:56.720
But I think my question is, are these glasses better than her backup glasses?
但我的问题是，这副眼镜比她的备用眼镜好看吗？

648
00:32:57.640 --> 00:32:58.500
Oh, my gosh.
噢，天哪。

649
00:32:58.720 --> 00:33:00.120
Because I thought she looked cute.
因为我觉得她看起来很可爱。

650
00:33:00.500 --> 00:33:03.480
Greg said in the commentary, this was, like, a big thing for Greg.
格雷格在评论音轨里说过，这对格雷格来说可是一件大事。

651
00:33:03.480 --> 00:33:09.220
He really, really wanted Pam, when she wasn't at work or somewhere out and about, that she wore glasses.
他真的非常希望潘在不在工作或外出的时候，能戴上眼镜。

652
00:33:09.560 --> 00:33:13.220
And whenever you could see Pam with her glasses, Greg just loved it.
只要你能看到潘戴着眼镜，格雷格就会特别喜欢。

653
00:33:13.560 --> 00:33:14.600
It's so funny.
太搞笑了。

654
00:33:14.800 --> 00:33:15.920
I loved wearing them.
我以前很喜欢戴。

655
00:33:16.000 --> 00:33:17.840
Now I have to wear glasses all the time.
现在我不得不一直戴着眼镜了。

656
00:33:17.920 --> 00:33:19.080
But it was fun.
但那挺有意思的。

657
00:33:19.560 --> 00:33:21.700
I loved the scene between Andy and Pam.
我很喜欢安迪和潘之间的那场戏。

658
00:33:21.840 --> 00:33:24.620
I thought it was hilarious when he was like, I was kind of doing your job.
我觉得当他说“我有点在做你的工作”时，简直太爆笑了。

659
00:33:24.620 --> 00:33:26.600
And she goes, my job?
然后她说，我的工作？

660
00:33:26.800 --> 00:33:28.780
My job is to get married in the morning.
我的工作是早上结婚。

661
00:33:28.940 --> 00:33:30.180
That's my job.
这就是我的工作。

662
00:33:32.140 --> 00:33:39.060
Veda shared in the commentary that there were a lot of alternate takes where you guys didn't reference balls and scrotum so much.
维达在评论音轨里分享说，有很多备用镜头里你们并没有那么多关于蛋蛋和阴囊的梗。

663
00:33:39.180 --> 00:33:39.540
Oh.
哦。

664
00:33:39.660 --> 00:33:42.720
But that you ultimately used most of the references.
但你们最终还是用了大部分的梗。

665
00:33:43.040 --> 00:33:50.080
And then Randy and her talked about the fact that our show pushed the standards and practices limit almost weekly.
然后兰迪和她谈到，我们的节目几乎每周都在挑战广电审查的极限。

666
00:33:50.440 --> 00:33:52.000
So I counted, Jenna.
所以我数了一下，珍娜。

667
00:33:52.520 --> 00:33:53.660
Oh, my gosh.
噢，天哪。

668
00:33:53.660 --> 00:34:00.440
In this episode, we say scrotum five times, balls one time, and penis one time.
在这集里，我们说了五次阴囊，一次蛋蛋，还有一次阴茎。

669
00:34:00.760 --> 00:34:02.060
That's not very many.
这其实不算太多。

670
00:34:02.260 --> 00:34:02.700
I know.
我知道。

671
00:34:02.800 --> 00:34:04.340
I was like, that's not that bad.
我当时就想，这没那么糟糕嘛。

672
00:34:04.340 --> 00:34:06.300
It's not as bad as when Phyllis got flashed.
这可没有菲利丝被暴露狂吓到那次那么糟。

673
00:34:06.600 --> 00:34:07.160
No.
确实。

674
00:34:07.520 --> 00:34:12.800
Well, ultimately, Andy is going to spend the night in Pam's room on her floor.
总之，安迪接下来要在潘的房间地板上过夜。

675
00:34:13.380 --> 00:34:17.380
And Michael is going to spend the night in the vending machine area.
而迈克尔要在自动售货机区域过夜。

676
00:34:17.840 --> 00:34:20.880
Because Dwight has a lady, there's a sock on the doorknob.
因为德怀特有女伴了，门把手上挂了袜子。

677
00:34:21.700 --> 00:34:22.640
Location alert.
外景地警报。

678
00:34:22.640 --> 00:34:24.880
If you can call it a location.
如果那也能算是个外景地的话。

679
00:34:25.720 --> 00:34:30.600
That vending machine area was actually an unused office at the hotel.
那个自动售货机区域实际上是酒店里一间闲置的办公室。

680
00:34:30.600 --> 00:34:37.360
And Michael Gallenberg's team had to dress it to look like an ice machine vending machine nook.
迈克尔·盖伦伯格的团队必须把它布置得像一个制冰机和自动售货机的角落。

681
00:34:38.120 --> 00:34:39.180
Here's my question.
我的问题来了。

682
00:34:39.980 --> 00:34:42.180
Where do you get an ice machine?
你从哪儿弄来一台制冰机？

683
00:34:42.560 --> 00:34:44.740
Like a hotel ice machine?
就像酒店那种制冰机？

684
00:34:44.860 --> 00:34:46.040
Like, who do you call?
比如，你给谁打电话？

685
00:34:46.480 --> 00:34:46.960
Where?
去哪儿弄？

686
00:34:47.120 --> 00:34:47.840
What is that?
那是什么东西？

687
00:34:47.980 --> 00:34:48.740
How do you do that?
这到底是怎么做到的？

688
00:34:49.300 --> 00:34:49.980
I'll tell you what.
我跟你说吧。

689
00:34:50.060 --> 00:34:54.720
If anyone knows where to get an industrial-sized ice machine, it's our team at the office.
如果有人知道去哪儿弄工业级的制冰机，那肯定是我们办公室的团队。

690
00:34:55.200 --> 00:34:55.680
Clearly.
显而易见。

691
00:34:56.500 --> 00:34:59.900
Oh, I want to say, I do believe that's filled with fakie ice.
哦，我想说，我相信那里面装的是假冰。

692
00:35:00.460 --> 00:35:01.340
Oh, it was.
哦，确实是的。

693
00:35:01.500 --> 00:35:02.760
They said that on the commentary.
他们在评论音轨里说过。

694
00:35:02.760 --> 00:35:03.840
It's fakie ice.
那是假冰。

695
00:35:03.980 --> 00:35:04.160
Yeah.
对。

696
00:35:04.760 --> 00:35:09.620
Well, now we're coming up on one of my favorite scenes in this whole episode.
好了，现在我们要看到整集中我最喜欢的场景之一了。

697
00:35:09.860 --> 00:35:11.220
Is it Kevin at the front desk?
是凯文在前台吗？

698
00:35:11.980 --> 00:35:12.300
Yes.
是的。

699
00:35:12.980 --> 00:35:13.940
Did you notice?
你注意到了吗？

700
00:35:14.080 --> 00:35:16.340
And I know this was just Brian being Brian.
而且我知道这只是布莱恩在展现真实的自己。

701
00:35:17.200 --> 00:35:20.020
How hard he hit that little ding bell.
他敲那声小叮当铃的声音可真响啊。

702
00:35:20.680 --> 00:35:22.920
It scared the crap out of those ladies.
把那些女士们吓得魂飞魄散。

703
00:35:23.680 --> 00:35:25.100
Kevin is looking for his shoes.
凯文在找他的鞋子。

704
00:35:25.440 --> 00:35:28.580
He left them outside his hotel room to be polished.
他把鞋子放在酒店房间外面让人擦洗。

705
00:35:29.180 --> 00:35:35.340
But the hotel manager, the amazing Nicholas Schaefer, who plays the hotel manager.
但是酒店经理，也就是饰演酒店经理的了不起的尼古拉斯·谢弗。

706
00:35:35.520 --> 00:35:36.620
He's so good.
他演得太棒了。

707
00:35:37.260 --> 00:35:43.540
Informs Kevin that they were so smelly that they made the decision to incinerate them.
通知凯文说，鞋子太臭了，他们决定将其焚毁。

708
00:35:43.720 --> 00:35:45.480
It was a safety issue, Jenna.
这是一个安全问题，珍娜。

709
00:35:45.720 --> 00:35:46.680
It was a safety issue.
这是一个安全问题。

710
00:35:46.960 --> 00:35:50.960
The only thing missing to me in this scene is Angela Martin in the background,
在我看来，这场戏里唯一缺少的就是背景里的安吉拉·马丁，

711
00:35:51.220 --> 00:35:54.240
smiling ear to ear, feeling so affirmed.
笑得合不拢嘴，感到大受肯定。

712
00:35:55.700 --> 00:35:58.780
And she's been talking about Kevin's smelly feet for years.
而且她多年来一直在抱怨凯文的脚臭。

713
00:35:59.060 --> 00:36:00.740
Oh, Angela is delighted.
哦，安吉拉太高兴了。

714
00:36:01.480 --> 00:36:03.060
She is so happy.
她太开心了。

715
00:36:03.300 --> 00:36:04.820
Somewhere she's so happy.
在某个地方她肯定高兴坏了。

716
00:36:05.340 --> 00:36:10.240
Well, the idea that they were going to have to burn Kevin's shoes because they were so smelly
嗯，他们因为凯文的鞋子太臭而不得不烧掉它们的这个创意，

717
00:36:10.240 --> 00:36:11.960
was our writer, Charlie Grandy.
是我们的编剧查理·格兰迪想出来的。

718
00:36:12.340 --> 00:36:16.120
And my friend, Michelle Gunn, who played the front desk clerk,
我的朋友米歇尔·冈恩，她在剧中饰演前台接待员，

719
00:36:16.540 --> 00:36:20.020
she told me that she improvised the line,
她告诉我，那句台词是她即兴发挥的，

720
00:36:20.590 --> 00:36:22.880
we can offer you a complimentary breakfaSt.
我们可以为您提供免费早餐。

721
00:36:24.240 --> 00:36:25.180
But get this, Angela.
但你听这个，安吉拉。

722
00:36:25.600 --> 00:36:28.420
Do you know how she got the idea to improvise that line?
你知道她是怎么想出即兴说那句台词的吗？

723
00:36:28.880 --> 00:36:29.120
No.
不知道。

724
00:36:29.440 --> 00:36:32.740
This is very similar to how you created Sprinkles.
这和当年你创造小雪球（Sprinkles）的过程非常相似。

725
00:36:33.600 --> 00:36:38.880
She was doodling on a Post-it note at the front desk as a bit of business.
她在前台当成动作戏份，在便签纸上随手涂鸦。

726
00:36:39.180 --> 00:36:44.560
And she was writing comp breakfast to room on the Post-it note.
她在便签纸上写着给房间免单早餐。

727
00:36:44.560 --> 00:36:53.100
And she said on one of the takes, Paul Feig just let the camera keep rolling for a really long time
她说在其中一个镜头里，保罗·费格让摄像机持续拍摄了很长很长时间，

728
00:36:53.100 --> 00:36:54.120
after the manager.
就在经理说完之后。

729
00:36:54.380 --> 00:36:56.040
That's what they would do on our show.
我们的节目向来都是这样的。

730
00:36:56.260 --> 00:36:56.760
Yes.
是的。

731
00:36:57.020 --> 00:37:00.380
So after the manager told Kevin that they burned his shoes,
所以在经理告诉凯文他们把他的鞋子烧了之后，

732
00:37:00.700 --> 00:37:03.020
there was just this very long pause.
现场出现了一段非常长的沉默。

733
00:37:03.200 --> 00:37:07.180
And so Michelle saw her sticky note and said,
于是米歇尔看到了她的便签纸，说道，

734
00:37:07.320 --> 00:37:09.340
we can offer you a complimentary breakfaSt.
我们可以为您提供免费早餐。

735
00:37:09.960 --> 00:37:12.920
And then Brian improvised, okay.
然后布莱恩即兴回应说，好吧。

736
00:37:13.860 --> 00:37:18.760
And she said it felt so good to be a guest actor on the show
她说，作为剧组的客串演员感觉太棒了，

737
00:37:18.760 --> 00:37:20.820
and get to contribute in such a fun way.
能以如此有趣的方式做出贡献。

738
00:37:21.020 --> 00:37:23.080
She said our show was really special like that
她说我们的剧真的很特别，

739
00:37:23.080 --> 00:37:24.420
because she's been on other things.
因为她也参演过其他作品。

740
00:37:24.820 --> 00:37:27.540
And she was like, you know, at this point,
当时的情况是，你知道的，

741
00:37:27.680 --> 00:37:28.920
she had done several scenes
到这个时候她已经拍了好几场戏了，

742
00:37:28.920 --> 00:37:31.960
and she had been working with Paul Feig now for a couple of days.
而且她和保罗·费格已经合作了好几天。

743
00:37:32.200 --> 00:37:33.940
And she was like, I don't know.
当时她心里想，我不知道。

744
00:37:33.940 --> 00:37:35.560
I feel like this would be okay.
我觉得这样做应该没问题吧。

745
00:37:36.620 --> 00:37:37.940
I just love that.
我太喜欢这个了。

746
00:37:38.160 --> 00:37:41.880
That just goes to show again how our show was so welcoming
这再次证明了我们的剧组是多么热情包容，

747
00:37:41.880 --> 00:37:43.460
and such a creative collaboration.
又是多么具有创造力的合作团队。

748
00:37:43.460 --> 00:37:44.560
And I love it.
我太喜欢了。

749
00:37:45.400 --> 00:37:48.340
Well, the next scene is Dwight wrapping things up with Isabel.
嗯，下一个镜头是德怀特和伊莎贝尔做收尾工作。

750
00:37:48.520 --> 00:37:50.300
She slept over in his room.
她在他的房间里过夜了。

751
00:37:50.780 --> 00:37:52.500
Michael is waiting out in the hallway.
迈克尔正在走廊外面等着。

752
00:37:52.800 --> 00:37:54.620
This made me laugh so hard, Jenna.
这让我笑得前仰后合，珍娜。

753
00:37:54.840 --> 00:37:55.960
I got so tickled.
我真的快笑死了。

754
00:37:56.460 --> 00:37:58.560
As he walks up, Michael says,
他走过来时，迈克尔说：

755
00:37:58.700 --> 00:38:00.240
it's about damn time.
这特么也太慢了吧。

756
00:38:00.380 --> 00:38:02.480
I haven't gone to the bathroom in a day and a half.
我都有一点半没去洗手间了。

757
00:38:02.480 --> 00:38:03.160
I know.
我知道。

758
00:38:03.440 --> 00:38:04.700
I thought the same thing.
我也是这么想的。

759
00:38:04.980 --> 00:38:08.140
I was like, you've been around a lot of restrooMs.
当时我想，你身边明明有很多洗手间啊。

760
00:38:08.420 --> 00:38:10.400
I mean, surely there's one off the lobby.
我是说，大厅附近肯定有一个吧。

761
00:38:10.700 --> 00:38:12.840
I think it meant he hadn't gone gone.
我觉得他的意思是没去上过大号。

762
00:38:13.060 --> 00:38:13.820
Do you know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吧？

763
00:38:14.000 --> 00:38:15.260
Oh, he hasn't.
哦，他确实没去。

764
00:38:15.440 --> 00:38:16.260
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

765
00:38:16.760 --> 00:38:18.120
He hasn't gone number two.
他一直没解大号。

766
00:38:18.460 --> 00:38:18.780
Right.
没错。

767
00:38:19.160 --> 00:38:20.820
He hasn't had a private space.
他一直没有私人空间。

768
00:38:21.020 --> 00:38:22.040
He hasn't.
确实没有。

769
00:38:22.180 --> 00:38:23.620
And that just cracked me up.
这真的把我逗乐了。

770
00:38:23.700 --> 00:38:24.860
He's so grumpy about it.
他为此感到非常暴躁。

771
00:38:25.240 --> 00:38:28.460
They then go to breakfast and Michael is so disgusted.
他们接着去吃早餐，迈克尔感到非常嫌弃。

772
00:38:28.720 --> 00:38:31.960
Look at how Steve looks at Rain as Dwight.
看史蒂夫看着雷恩饰演的德怀特时的眼神。

773
00:38:31.960 --> 00:38:33.120
It is so funny.
真的太搞笑了。

774
00:38:33.620 --> 00:38:35.740
Dwight is just shoveling all this food in his mouth.
德怀特一个劲地把这些食物往嘴里塞。

775
00:38:36.200 --> 00:38:41.580
They shared in the DVD commentary that Phil Shea had like a hundred pancakes ready to go.
他们在DVD随片讲评里分享过，菲尔·希尔准备了一百张左右的煎饼随时待命。

776
00:38:41.720 --> 00:38:44.140
Because you know how Rain was in those scenes as Dwight.
因为你知道雷恩在那些戏里演德怀特时是怎样的。

777
00:38:44.260 --> 00:38:44.920
He eats.
他特别能吃。

778
00:38:45.100 --> 00:38:46.680
He was going to destroy it.
他打算把它们全消灭掉。

779
00:38:46.800 --> 00:38:47.020
Yeah.
对啊。

780
00:38:47.060 --> 00:38:48.980
Like he would eat a lot.
就好像他会吃很多东西。

781
00:38:49.160 --> 00:38:51.360
That was part of his like character thing.
那是他角色设定的一部分。

782
00:38:51.580 --> 00:38:54.000
Remember when he ate all those bananas and he got sick?
还记得他吃掉所有那些香蕉然后生病的事吗？

783
00:38:54.340 --> 00:38:55.060
I do.
我记得。

784
00:38:55.060 --> 00:38:58.160
But then they just sort of made it part of who Dwight was.
但后来他们就把这融入了德怀特的性格特点中。

785
00:38:58.360 --> 00:39:01.520
Dwight even says he's ravenous after a night of lovemaking.
德怀特甚至说他在一番云雨之后饿得像狼一样。

786
00:39:01.760 --> 00:39:02.780
What about you?
你呢？

787
00:39:02.980 --> 00:39:05.860
And then this is when we hear about Michael's European girlfriend.
然后这就是我们听到迈克尔的欧洲女友的时候。

788
00:39:05.860 --> 00:39:08.340
Yeah, exactly.
对，没错。

789
00:39:08.860 --> 00:39:10.480
I have some news.
我有个消息。

790
00:39:10.760 --> 00:39:12.720
It's time to go to the church.
是时候去教堂了。

791
00:39:13.540 --> 00:39:15.340
And I've got a location alert.
我有一个外景地提醒。

792
00:39:15.980 --> 00:39:21.160
If you are interested in getting married somewhere in Sherman Oaks, California,
如果你有兴趣在加州谢尔曼奥克斯的某个地方结婚，

793
00:39:21.160 --> 00:39:26.680
and you need doors big enough to fit a horse, you can head on over to the Church of the Chimes
而且你需要能容纳一匹马进出的足够大的门，你可以去谢尔曼奥克斯的钟声教堂，

794
00:39:26.680 --> 00:39:28.220
on Magnolia Boulevard.
位于木兰大道上。

795
00:39:28.680 --> 00:39:31.960
We shot at this church on two different Saturdays.
我们在这座教堂拍了两不同的周六。

796
00:39:32.180 --> 00:39:36.660
I mentioned last week we had to shoot on Saturdays because that was the only day that
我上周提过，我们必须在周六拍摄，因为那是唯一一天

797
00:39:36.660 --> 00:39:41.920
we could get every single guest star together in the same room at the same time.
我们能让每一位客串演员同时聚在同一个房间里。

798
00:39:42.260 --> 00:39:47.840
The little ready room that I get ready with with my bridesmaids and my mom,
我和伴娘还有我妈妈一起准备的那个小备用间，

799
00:39:47.840 --> 00:39:51.180
that was one of the Sunday school classrooms at the church.
其实是教堂里的一间主日学校教室。

800
00:39:51.180 --> 00:39:55.260
And they just kind of redressed it to look like a bride's ready room.
他们只是稍微重新布置了一下，让它看起来像新娘准备室。

801
00:39:55.860 --> 00:39:58.320
And I don't know if you remember this about the location.
我不知道你对这个拍摄地还有没有印象。

802
00:39:58.420 --> 00:39:59.880
We kind of talked about this with Greg.
我们和格雷格聊过这个。

803
00:40:00.280 --> 00:40:02.340
We didn't have trailers on site.
我们在现场没有保姆车。

804
00:40:02.800 --> 00:40:05.640
So we just all kind of hung around on that patio.
所以大家就都聚在那边的露台上。

805
00:40:05.680 --> 00:40:09.820
And we talked about how Ed and Creed were playing music.
我们还聊到埃德和克里德当时在弹音乐。

806
00:40:10.520 --> 00:40:11.800
Yeah, Ed brought his banjo.
对，埃德带了他的班卓琴。

807
00:40:11.940 --> 00:40:13.160
I think Creed had his mandolin.
我想克里德带了他的曼陀林。

808
00:40:13.460 --> 00:40:15.120
They had a little jam session.
他们来了一场小型即兴演奏。

809
00:40:15.120 --> 00:40:17.040
And there was that grassy area.
那边还有一片草地。

810
00:40:17.040 --> 00:40:20.420
You see it in a few shots from the church scenes.
你在教堂场景的几个镜头里能看到。

811
00:40:20.660 --> 00:40:22.060
And we just hung out there.
我们就一直在那里闲逛。

812
00:40:22.160 --> 00:40:23.200
It was really fun.
真的很有意思。

813
00:40:23.200 --> 00:40:26.820
And it's one of my fondest memories of the whole run of the show.
这也是我整部剧拍摄期间最美好的回忆之一。

814
00:40:27.400 --> 00:40:30.060
Now, do you remember when the paparazzi showed up?
话说，你还记得狗仔队出现的时候吗？

815
00:40:30.980 --> 00:40:32.420
Oh, yeah, I do.
哦，对，我记得。

816
00:40:32.740 --> 00:40:38.060
Yeah, they were trying to take pictures of me and John in our wedding outfits.
对，他们当时想拍我和约翰穿着结婚礼服的照片。

817
00:40:38.700 --> 00:40:39.680
Yeah, they did.
没错，他们拍了。

818
00:40:39.940 --> 00:40:42.680
You know, the church is on a kind of a busy corner.
你知道的，那个教堂在一个相对繁忙的街角。

819
00:40:42.680 --> 00:40:48.360
And Randy talked about it, that it was hard to make it private because it was on the corner
兰迪也说过，要保密很难，因为它就在一个

820
00:40:48.360 --> 00:40:49.240
of an intersection.
十字路口拐角处。

821
00:40:49.640 --> 00:40:51.120
So guess what, Jenna?
所以你猜怎么着，珍娜？

822
00:40:51.460 --> 00:40:56.160
They shared on the commentary, and you probably remember this, that you and Paul Lieberstein
他们在评论音轨里分享说，你大概也记得，你和保罗·利伯斯坦

823
00:40:56.160 --> 00:40:58.700
decided to stage a photo.
决定摆拍一张照片。

824
00:40:59.480 --> 00:41:01.100
Yes, oh my gosh.
对，天哪。

825
00:41:01.240 --> 00:41:02.380
Yes, I remember that.
是的，我记得。

826
00:41:03.000 --> 00:41:10.140
Yeah, we thought, what if we do like a fakey, we were going to pretend like we were shooting
对，我们当时想，如果我们来个假的会怎么样，我们打算假装我们在拍

827
00:41:10.140 --> 00:41:17.100
a scene, and we were going to have me and Paul, dressed as Toby, run out of the church
一场戏，让我和打扮成托比的保罗

828
00:41:17.100 --> 00:41:22.280
holding hands as if we had gotten married or as if he was stealing me from the wedding.
手拉手跑出教堂，就好像我们结婚了，或者好像他把我从婚礼上抢走了似得。

829
00:41:22.280 --> 00:41:29.000
We even had the camera guys pretend to shoot us so it would look like we were shooting,
我们甚至让摄像师假装拍我们，好让它看起来像是在拍摄，

830
00:41:29.000 --> 00:41:34.380
and we wanted the paparazzi to take pictures of that so they wouldn't get a real spoiler.
我们想让狗仔队拍那个，这样他们就不会拍到真正的剧透了。

831
00:41:34.920 --> 00:41:35.940
Well, they did.
嗯，他们真的拍了。

832
00:41:36.140 --> 00:41:39.340
You guys clearly ran out the front doors and you hugged.
你们俩确实跑出了前门还拥抱了。

833
00:41:39.560 --> 00:41:40.540
There's like an embrace.
就好像有个拥抱。

834
00:41:40.800 --> 00:41:44.700
I found the paparazzi photo that ended up in a tabloid.
我找到了最后登上小报的狗仔队照片。

835
00:41:44.860 --> 00:41:45.340
No.
不会吧。

836
00:41:45.560 --> 00:41:46.460
Yes, I did.
真的，我找到了。

837
00:41:46.660 --> 00:41:47.800
I'll put it in stories.
我会把它发到快拍里。

838
00:41:48.080 --> 00:41:51.100
Fakey photo of Pam and Toby hugging.
帕姆和托比拥抱的摆拍照。

839
00:41:51.100 --> 00:41:53.940
And it's really funny, Jenna, because on the internet, people were like,
真的太搞笑了，珍娜，因为在网上，大家都在说：

840
00:41:54.080 --> 00:41:56.460
I'm sorry, why is Pam in a wedding dress?
不好意思，为什么帕姆穿着婚纱？

841
00:41:56.540 --> 00:41:57.400
Why is she hugging Toby?
为什么她要拥抱托比？

842
00:41:57.540 --> 00:41:58.160
What's happening?
这到底是怎么回事？

843
00:41:58.820 --> 00:42:01.380
Oh my gosh, that is so funny.
哦天哪，太好笑了。

844
00:42:01.480 --> 00:42:02.640
I did not remember that part.
我不记得这一段了。

845
00:42:02.780 --> 00:42:04.240
I did not remember that it worked.
我不记得它居然成功了。

846
00:42:04.620 --> 00:42:05.360
It did.
确实成功了。

847
00:42:06.040 --> 00:42:08.000
At the church, everyone is arriving.
在教堂，大家都陆续到了。

848
00:42:09.120 --> 00:42:11.800
Phyllis's outfit is amazing.
菲利斯的行头太惊艳了。

849
00:42:12.520 --> 00:42:14.180
Giant hat, many feathers.
巨大的帽子，好多羽毛。

850
00:42:14.980 --> 00:42:18.100
I mean, it's a whole like pink suit, hat, the whole thing.
我是说，整套粉色套装、帽子，一应俱全。

851
00:42:18.680 --> 00:42:22.340
Mindy, I guess, had really wanted the character of Phyllis to go all out.
我想明迪真的很想让菲利斯的角色全力以赴。

852
00:42:22.500 --> 00:42:28.640
Like she wanted a huge like fashion statement outfit as if she was going to one of those big
就像她想要一件非常夸张的时尚声明服装，就好像她要去参加那些盛大的

853
00:42:28.640 --> 00:42:29.400
southern weddings.
南方婚礼一样。

854
00:42:29.940 --> 00:42:36.800
Well, speaking of going all out, Kevin shows up with his hair piece, but then he doesn't
说到全力以赴，凯文戴着他的假发出现了，但他却

855
00:42:36.800 --> 00:42:37.420
have his shoes.
没有穿鞋。

856
00:42:37.420 --> 00:42:42.720
And this is where we see that he has made shoes out of a couple of tissue boxes.
正是在这里，我们看到他用几个纸巾盒做成了鞋子。

857
00:42:43.380 --> 00:42:49.860
When he walks in and sits down next to Oscar and Angela, Jenna, we had so much fun in this
当他走进来坐在奥斯卡和安吉拉旁边时，珍娜，我们在这一场戏里

858
00:42:49.860 --> 00:42:50.200
scene.
玩得太开心了。

859
00:42:50.380 --> 00:42:54.660
It is such a small moment, but I want you to know it was so delicious.
这是一个非常小的瞬间，但我想让你们知道它太美妙了。

860
00:42:55.120 --> 00:42:59.480
When my character looks over at him and goes, oh my God.
当我的角色转头看着他，说，噢，天哪。

861
00:43:00.100 --> 00:43:01.920
And then Oscar looks at him.
然后奥斯卡看着他。

862
00:43:02.100 --> 00:43:03.260
We just had a blaSt.
我们简直玩嗨了。

863
00:43:03.920 --> 00:43:06.200
We got a fan question from Amy A.
我们收到了来自路易斯安那州的

864
00:43:06.320 --> 00:43:06.860
in Louisiana.
艾米·A. 的粉丝提问。

865
00:43:06.860 --> 00:43:12.900
Anna, who came up with the idea for Kevin to wear tissue boxes to replace his shoes and
安娜，是谁想出让凯文穿纸巾盒来代替鞋子的主意，它们是用什么做的？

866
00:43:12.900 --> 00:43:13.980
what were they made of?
基本上，他们是怎么制作这些东西的？

867
00:43:14.280 --> 00:43:15.740
How did they make them, basically?
简而言之，它们是如何制作的？

868
00:43:16.340 --> 00:43:22.560
So it was Greg who came up with the idea of Kevin using the tissue boxes and they were
所以是格雷格想出了让凯文使用纸巾盒的主意，它们是

869
00:43:22.560 --> 00:43:26.400
constructed using extra large Kleenex boxes.
用特大号舒洁纸巾盒构建的。

870
00:43:27.100 --> 00:43:30.020
And Randy Cordray said that's an actual thing.
兰迪·科德雷说这真是个东西。

871
00:43:30.200 --> 00:43:32.240
This was not a fakie construction.
这不是虚构的道具。

872
00:43:32.240 --> 00:43:35.980
They just bought giant tissue boxes.
他们只是买了巨大的纸巾盒。

873
00:43:36.460 --> 00:43:39.140
Where do you buy tissue boxes that big?
你在哪儿能买到那么大的纸巾盒？

874
00:43:39.320 --> 00:43:44.220
I don't know that, but they were fitted with flip-flops inside.
我不知道，但它们的内部安装了人字拖。

875
00:43:44.320 --> 00:43:47.820
So that's how they stayed on Brian's feet.
所以这就是它们能固定在布莱恩脚上的方式。

876
00:43:48.200 --> 00:43:53.880
He said we had to make about 10 pairs of them because they did get beat up pretty quickly.
他说我们必须制作大约 10 双，因为它们确实很快就会损坏。

877
00:43:56.180 --> 00:44:00.440
Now you're going to see a bunch of little vignette scenes of everybody at the church.
现在你会看到教堂里每个人的许多小插曲镜头。

878
00:44:00.440 --> 00:44:05.700
Michael has a talking head where he shares what he got Jim and Pam as their wedding gift.
迈克尔有一段单人访谈，分享了他送给吉姆和帕姆的结婚礼物是什么。

879
00:44:06.160 --> 00:44:11.300
It's, it's, um, I am at a loss of words.
这，这个，嗯，我无话可说。

880
00:44:11.500 --> 00:44:13.060
It's a, it's a painting.
这是个，这是幅画。

881
00:44:13.380 --> 00:44:14.440
He made it himself.
是他自己画的。

882
00:44:14.800 --> 00:44:16.240
He did it from memory.
他是凭记忆画的。

883
00:44:16.580 --> 00:44:17.060
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

884
00:44:17.460 --> 00:44:17.800
Right?
对吧？

885
00:44:18.000 --> 00:44:21.220
He also has another version of this painting where they're nude.
这幅画他还有另一个全裸的版本。

886
00:44:21.380 --> 00:44:22.540
He's keeping that for himself.
他要自己留着。

887
00:44:22.740 --> 00:44:23.040
Right.
没错。

888
00:44:23.440 --> 00:44:23.900
Awesome.
太棒了。

889
00:44:24.200 --> 00:44:24.600
What?
什么？

890
00:44:25.260 --> 00:44:26.720
But here's a little tidbit.
但这里有个小花絮。

891
00:44:26.720 --> 00:44:31.980
If you go to seven minutes, 35 seconds during this talking head, you'll notice that the stained
如果你在这段单人访谈的 7 分 35 秒处观看，你会发现他身后的彩色

892
00:44:31.980 --> 00:44:34.780
glass window behind him is totally dark.
玻璃窗完全是黑的。

893
00:44:35.020 --> 00:44:38.440
There's no light coming through it, but he's lit up so bright.
没有光透过它，但他却被照得非常亮。

894
00:44:38.440 --> 00:44:43.560
It's because you guys, we filmed this at night, but it was made to look like daytime,
这是因为大家，我们是晚上拍摄的，但它被做成了白天白的样子，

895
00:44:43.560 --> 00:44:46.100
but you can't hide the stained glass.
但你无法掩盖彩色玻璃。

896
